# .gitignore for the PUBLIC repo (v2, 2026-09-03).
#
# Deliberately stricter than the working repo's. The working repo is private and
# local forever, so its ignore file only has to keep the tree tidy. This one is
# a disclosure control, and it is the LAST line of defence rather than the first
# - the build script never copies excluded folders in at all, so anything this
# file catches represents a build-script gap worth fixing at source.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated --
Outputs/
**/Logs/
*.log
node_modules/
package-lock.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ------------------------------------------------------- backups and scratch --
# git is the backup. A .bak beside a tracked file is both redundant and a way
# for a pre-correction version of a file to ship after the file was fixed.
*.bak
*.backup
*-backup
*.pre-*
*.orig
*.tmp
working/
scratch/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- credentials --
# Nothing credential-shaped, ever. Belt and braces: the scan checks content too,
# because a token in a .py file would sail past every pattern below.
*.env
.env*
*secret*
*credential*
*token*
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
token-cache.json
*-token-cache.json
flow-bridge.config.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------ machine-local --
# Tunnel hostnames and per-machine config identify the machine and, in the case
# of a devtunnel URL, are a live ingress to it.
*.local.txt
*.local.json
denylist.local.txt
_commit-msg.txt
_lessons-known-keys.txt
.lesson-receipts/
allow.local.txt
excludes.local.txt
sanitize.local.txt
skill-menu.cache.json

# --------------------------------------------------------- superseded drafts --
# Old drafts and staging artefacts that the build already excludes.
SS_SKILL*
_v050_*
AUTORUN.ps1

# --------------------------------------------------- engagement and client --
# Present as a backstop only. The build script excludes these by name; if one
# ever appears here it means the copy step let something through.
Quarantine/
EnvironmentDiscovery/
**/state-apportionment/
**/intercompany-eliminations/
**/tax-client-emails/
**/alteryx-to-python/
**/je-builder/
**/deck-builder/
**/power-automate/
**/tax-provision-report-replication/

# ----------------------------------------------------------- not this repo --
# AUTORUN is a forbidden execution fallback, kept on disk and out of git so
# nobody reads its presence as endorsement.
autorun/
